  "id": "stimulation-effects",
  "term": "stimulation effects",
  "definition": "Stimulation effects are the outcomes produced by brain stimulation, arising from the volume of nearby tissue activated by the electrical current rather than only the exact electrode contact point. Because that activated area can overlap multiple brain structures, the observed effects may be a mixture of influences from those different structures.",
